              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Few situations are more stressful than being broken down on the side of the highway with a loaded trailer, a tight delivery window, and traffic flying by.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For owner-operators and fleet drivers alike, a breakdown isn't just an inconvenience; it's lost income, delayed customers, and mounting pressure by the minute.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Knowing how semi truck road service works, when to call for help, and what to expect can make a difficult situation far more manageable. At Sun State International, our goal is simple: help drivers get back on the road safely, efficiently, and with as little downtime as possible.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-what-is-road-service",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What Is Semi Truck Road Service?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "what-is-road-service"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-what-is-road-service-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Semi truck road service provides on-site assistance when a commercial truck experiences a mechanical issue away from the shop. Instead of towing the vehicle immediately, trained technicians assess the problem and complete repairs roadside when possible. This type of roadside truck service is especially valuable for issues that don't require full-shop equipment but still stop you from continuing your route.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-what-is-road-service-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Common services include:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-what-is-road-service-3",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Battery replacement or jump-starts"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Air line and hose repairs"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Electrical diagnostics"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Minor brake repairs"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Belt, clamp, or sensor replacements"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-what-is-road-service-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For many drivers, road service is the difference between hours of downtime and getting back on schedule.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-staying-safe",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Staying Safe While Waiting for Truck Breakdown Assistance",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "staying-safe"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-staying-safe-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "While waiting for truck breakdown assistance, safety should always come first:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-staying-safe-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Pull as far off the roadway as possible"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Activate hazard lights immediately"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Set reflective triangles if conditions allow"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Stay inside the cab unless it's unsafe"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Communicate your exact location clearly"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-staying-safe-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A prepared driver is safer and easier for service teams to reach.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/semi-truck-road-service/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Sun State International service and parts location where road service teams are dispatched from"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-when-to-call",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When to Call for Emergency Truck Repair",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "when-to-call"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-when-to-call-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Not every issue can, or should, be handled roadside. Knowing when to call for emergency truck repair helps protect both your truck and your safety. You should request road service if:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-when-to-call-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Warning lights indicate a non-catastrophic fault"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "The truck won't start due to electrical or battery issues"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "You experience air leaks affecting braking or suspension"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Minor mechanical issues prevent safe operation"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-when-to-call-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If there's major engine damage, severe brake failure, or a safety risk, towing to a service facility is often the best option. A professional road service team can help make that call quickly.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-bottom-line",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Roadside Truck Service Matters to Your Bottom Line",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "bottom-line"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-bottom-line-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Unplanned vehicle downtime can cost trucking operations hundreds of dollars per hour when factoring in lost productivity, labor, and missed loads. For owner-operators, that impact is even more personal.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-bottom-line-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Reliable truck breakdown assistance helps:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-bottom-line-3",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Minimize delivery delays"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Reduce towing expenses"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Protect long-term equipment health"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Keep drivers safer in high-traffic areas"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-bottom-line-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Road service isn't just about fixing the problem; it's about limiting the ripple effect that breakdowns cause.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
